## Task List
// The tasks are this project's own:  Task.
// This file adds their list, and the app:  adding a task, filtering the list, and editing what's selected.
// What's where, top to bottom:
//   the checklist:  the tasks, shown as the filter says
//   the app:  its menu, the new task's field, the list and the property editor
//   start
//   tests


## The checklist:  the tasks, each its own element inside it
// a viewable list:  `<task-list-checklist>`, around its tasks' `<task-list-task>`s
<spell-thing "checklist" template="viewable list of tasks">
	<property "showing" one-of="all, active or done" description="what it shows:  every task, the ones still to do, or the ones done" />
	// on the page, its tasks can be dragged to another place:  they move as the pointer does, gliding there
	<spell>
		- its items can be reordered immediately
		// each task, unless the filter hides it
		- to draw each item:
			if its showing is "active" and the task is done return nothing
			if its showing is "done" and the task is active return nothing
			return draw the task
		// empty:  says so
		- to draw its placeholder:
			return <div part="placeholder">Nothing to do</div>
	</spell>
</spell-thing>

// a task is in one checklist at a time
<spell>
	a task belongs to one checklist
</spell>


## The app:  its menu, the new task's field, the list, and the property editor
<spell-app "task list">
	<property "tasks">a new checklist</>
	<property "draft" description="what the new task's field holds:  the next task's title">text</>
	<property "active count">the length of (tasks in its tasks where it is active)</>

	<action "add the draft" description="the draft, as a new task at the end of the list;  the field empties">
		if its draft is "" return
		add (a new task with title = its draft, priority = normal) to its tasks
		clear its draft
	</action>

	<action "remove the done tasks">
		remove tasks in its tasks where it is done
	</action>

	// its menu, the new task's field, then the list beside the property editor
	// - the menu's buttons are icons, each with a tooltip
	// - the property editor edits every selected task at once:  a property they disagree on shows "Mixed"
	<spell>
		- to draw it:
			return <ui-container class="TaskList">
				<ui-menu>
					<ui-item kind="header">Task List</ui-item>
					<ui-item>{its active count + " to do"}</ui-item>
					<ui-menu position="right">
						<ui-item aria-label="All" selected={the showing of its tasks is "all"} onClick={set the showing of its tasks to "all"}>
							<ui-icon name="list"/>
							<ui-popup label="All" inverted size="small"/>
						</ui-item>
						<ui-item aria-label="To do" selected={the showing of its tasks is "active"} onClick={set the showing of its tasks to "active"}>
							<ui-icon name="square outline"/>
							<ui-popup label="To do" inverted size="small"/>
						</ui-item>
						<ui-item aria-label="Done" selected={the showing of its tasks is "done"} onClick={set the showing of its tasks to "done"}>
							<ui-icon name="check square outline"/>
							<ui-popup label="Done" inverted size="small"/>
						</ui-item>
						<ui-item aria-label="Remove done" onClick={remove the done tasks}>
							<ui-icon name="trash alternate outline"/>
							<ui-popup label="Remove the done tasks" inverted size="small"/>
						</ui-item>
					</ui-menu>
				</ui-menu>
				<ui-form value={it}>
					<div class="NewTask">
						<ui-input name="draft" placeholder="Something to do" aria-label="New task" fluid/>
						<ui-button color="primary" disabled={its draft is ""} onClick={add the draft}>Add</ui-button>
					</div>
				</ui-form>
				<ui-grid columns="2" stackable>
					{draw its tasks}
					<ui-property-editor label="Selected tasks" schema="task-list-task" value={the selection of its tasks}>
						<ui-property name="title"/>
						<ui-property name="priority"/>
						<ui-property name="done"/>
						<ui-property name="notes"/>
					</ui-property-editor>
				</ui-grid>
			</ui-container>
	</spell>
</spell-app>


## Start
<spell>
	set the showing of the tasks of the task list to all
	add (a new task with title = "Write the Task List example", priority = high, done = yes) to the tasks of the task list
	add (a new task with title = "Teach it to draw", priority = normal) to the tasks of the task list
	add (a new task with title = "Select some tasks, then edit them together", priority = normal) to the tasks of the task list
	add (a new task with title = "Drag tasks to reorder them", priority = low) to the tasks of the task list
	start the task list


	## Tests
	to test the filter
		set the tasks to a new checklist
		add (a new task with title = "a", done = yes) to the tasks
		add (a new task with title = "b") to the tasks
		the length of (tasks in the tasks where it is active) should be 1
</spell>
